      "line": 160,
      "why_it_matters": "An invalid operation in an authored packet can still produce a passing model/control proof, so the receipt does not establish that the declared operation vocabulary was followed. WML016 silently treats every token other than add or alter as subtract; MCL016 likewise treats every token other than backup as a forward cursor movement. A nonmutating probe replacing the existing subtract and forward tokens with invalid_operation passed both independent fixed expectations and packet expectations. Explicit vocabulary checks preserve the finite-case scope while rejecting malformed fixture steps.",
